        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: One Liberty Plaza, Lower Manhattan, Manhattan, New York City, United States\n- Buildings: U.S. Steel Building, Singer Building, City Investing Building, 1717 Broadway\n- Organizations: Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton LLP\n- Topics: skyscrapers, hotel height, headquarters\n\nFacts:\n- One Liberty Plaza, formerly the U.S. Steel Building, is a skyscraper in Lower Manhattan in New York City.\n- One Liberty Plaza stands on the site of the former Singer Building and the former City Investing Building.\n- The Singer Building was the tallest structure ever dismantled.\n- 1717 Broadway is a skyscraper in Manhattan, New York City, United States.\n- 1717 Broadway is 750 feet tall and is the tallest hotel in North America.\n- Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton LLP is an international law firm headquartered at One Liberty Plaza in New York City.",
